abstract: >-
  A private company has no continuously observable price, and between
  transactions its value is whatever its holders say it is. On the population of
  Level-3 private marks US registered funds filed from 2019Q4 to 2026Q2 -
  309,654 marks, no company list consulted - independent fund houses report the
  same private share a median of 12.1 percent apart, and 180.0 billion dollars
  of the 517.3 billion booked in these positions sits above a 24 percent spread.
  The unit of an independent valuation is the fund house rather than the legal
  trust that files: measured between registrants the same data give 0.004
  percent. The disagreement survives a Level-1 placebo, a subsample in which no
  house re-marked, and one lot whose entry price is disclosed and identical.
  What compresses it is a transaction, and only briefly.
